(BAS-55 - the empty-Otherwise example, LANGUAGE.md:306-318, verbatim: an
 `Otherwise,.` takes the inner if's else branch and does nothing with it,
 closing that chain, so the second `Otherwise` continues the outer if.
 Same result as two periods.
 Also covers: BAS-54 (an empty `Otherwise,.` closes an inner chain the
 same way a stacked period does).
